CFM will determine which parts are required to perform the Services and will provide all parts and materials (new, used Serviceable, or Rotable Parts). Title to parts and material furnished by CFM will pass to Customer upon incorporation in the Engine.

{CFM shall obtain written approval from Customer before installing any used Serviceable Parts on the Engine. For avoidance of doubt, Customer shall respond to CFM with a decision of approval or refusal within [days_for_answer] Day, any extra time spent on Customer communication per this paragraph should be added to the TAT.}

{[parties] shall obtain title in any used LLP that is removed from an Engine and which is replaced by new LLP pursuant to Customer's obligation under article [article]. For any other removed Parts, }

Customer shall retain title to removed Parts and such removed Parts shall be held at the DRS for [days] Days {[following_redelivery_of_the_Engine]}for the Customer to review and/or retrieve them. After such period, any Parts not retrieved by Customer become CFM property {[return]}.

{CFM shall inform Customer for the disposition of such removed Parts no later than [CFM_days_to_inform] Days before the end of the Period. After such Period, any Parts not retrieved by Customer become CFM property.}

CFM may elect to use parts from its Rotable Parts inventory to replace Customer’s repairable parts, which will be repaired by CFM at Customer’s expense. If such removed parts are later scrapped, condemned or determined to be non-repairable, or under limitation (such as, but not limited to a Customer Departure Record), {and [condition] otherwise covered under the FFP Workscope,} Customer will pay for the replacement part as detailed in the widget [widget], less any applicable exchange fee previously paid and the parts will be disposed of at no expense to Customer. 

Title to Rotable Parts furnished by CFM will pass to Customer upon incorporation in the Engine, and simultaneously, title to the parts replaced will pass to CFM.

Rotable Parts shall not be used to replace a Part coming from an Engine that has been subject to an accident or misuse.

{Prior to use Ratable Parts from its Ratable Parts inventory, CFM will request Customer's prior approval to be received by CFM within [days_from_request] Days from request. In case Customer fail to give its approval within [days_for_approval] Days, the guaranteed TAT will be extended accordingly.}

{Customer agrees to delegate approval to use Rotable Parts to CFM for non-LLP parts if the Rotable Part meets the following cumulative criteria : [criteria]}

{CFM agrees to request from Customer approval to use Rotable Parts or a used Serviceable Part in an Engine to replace non-LLP parts. Customer acknowledges that if the relevant Rotable Part meets the
following cumulative criteria it shall not unreasonably withhold its approval: [criteria_]}

{If Customer is unwilling to accept the use of Rotable Parts, or desires to provide his own parts, TAT target may have to be readjusted. In any case, parts from Customer’s own fleet or Customer Furnished Equipment shall be provided within [days] days after the Engine disassembly is completed, otherwise Rotable Parts will be provided.}

{For all Rotable Parts and used serviceable material that do not fulfil the above criteria, [Partie] shall obtain written approval from Customer before installing a part on the Engine.}

{[1] If Customer's fleet is operated under different conditions than the Operating Parameters or
subsequently Repaired to a different level than currently defined in the Eligible Workscope, the
guaranteed single engine EGT margin may be adjusted.}
{[2] All liquidated damages paid by CFM to Customer shall be made in the form of a credit to be
applied against the applicable final invoice amount.}
{[3]For the purpose of this Article, an "Eligible Workscope" means the following workscope: [workscope]}

{[1]The Guarantee will commence following the Engine's Performance Restoration Workscope, and will terminate when the Engine either: (i) requires a subsequent shop visit or (ii) exceeds the guaranteed EFH.}

{[1_bis]The Guarantee will commence following the Engine's Performance Restoration Workscope, and will terminate when the Engine exceeds the guaranteed EFH.}


{[2]The Engine must be removed for performance deterioration resulting from normal prolonged on­wing operation, with fewer than guaranteed TOW EFH. If the Engine is removed for any other reason, or is found to have suffered performance deterioration as a result of an identifiable cause other than normal prolonged on-wing operation (e.g. debris ingestion, faulty LRU's, mishandling or other actions/inactions not consistent with good practice) then the removal will net be eligible for the TOW guarantee.}

{[3]Customer required to, in accordance with the on-wing performance monitoring trends, (i) in a timely manner troubleshoot and correct where possible the adverse Engine performance reports and (ii) perform at appropriate regular intervals engine gas path water wash per the OEM Engme Shop Manual or equivalent Airframer's Manual.}

{[4]All liquidated damages paid by CFM to Customer shall be made in the form of a credit to be applied against the applicable final invoice amount.}

{[5]Operating Parameters: The Engine shall be operated under the conditions defined in Exhibit "Engines Covered". On an exceptional basis, CFM allows Customer to perform up to five percent (5%) of the take-offs with a higher thrust rating originally sold. If the Engine has performed more than five percent (5%) of the take-offs originally sold with a higher thrust rating, then the corresponding Time On Wing Guarantee level of this higher thrust rating will apply for this specific Engine.}

{[6]If Customer’s fleet is operated under different conditions than the Operating Parameters or subsequently Repaired to a different level than currently defined in the Repair Specification, the guaranteed single engine EGT margin may be adjusted (upward or downward).}

{[7]If Customer's fleet is operated under different conditions than the Operating Parameters or subsequently Repaired to a different level than currently defined in the Repair Specification, the guaranteed single engine EGT margin may be adjusted (upward or downward).}

{[8]Performance Restoration Workscope (or “PRW”) shall include, at a minimum, the following Services: (i) exposure and refurbishment of the Combustor and High Pressure Turbine modules of the Engine; (ii) evaluation (at the module level), and (as required based on hardware conditions and time since last refurbishment) cleaning and refurbishment of the Fan, Low Pressure Compressor, High Pressure Compressor and Low Pressure Turbine module flowpaths and seals; (iii) refurbishment of the EGT Indication System; and (iv) inspection and Test in accordance with the Component Maintenance Manual and refurbishment if required) of the Fuel Distribution and Airflow Control System components as recommended in CFM’s published documents.}

{[9] The Engine is Unserviceable due to EGT margin limitation resulting from normal prolonged on-wing
operation, prior to the TOW guarantee termination.}

{[10] If the Engine is removed for any other reason, or is found to have suffered performance deterioration
as a result of an identifiable cause other than normal prolonged on-wing operation (e.g . debris
ingestion, faulty Engine Controls and Accessories, mishandling, convenience, lease return, Aircraft
Accident, Aircraft Incident, or other actions/inactions not consistent with good practices), then the
removal will not be eligible for the TOW guarantee.}

{[11] Operating Parameters: The Engine shall be operated under the Operating Parameters, and in
accordance with the AFM.}

{[12] Customer is required to, in accordance with the on-wing performance monitoring trends, (i) in a
timely manner troubleshoot and correct where possible the adverse Engine performance reports
and (ii) perform at appropriate regular intervals Engine gas path water wash per the OEM Engine
Shop Manual or equivalent Airframer's Manual.}

Upon Delivery, CFM will notify Customer of any components or [missing_items] missing from the Engine. CFM will replace such missing items at Customer’s expense as Supplemental Services, unless:
- Customer notifies CFM in writing within [hours_days] [unit] after receiving CFM’s notice that Customer wishes to furnish such missing items;
- Customer delivers such missing items to the CFM Designated Repair Station within [weeks] weeks.  

{In order to complete the test cell run, in the event any component or Engine Controls and Accessories item is missing from the Engine, CFM may, at Customer’s request, fit its own item if available. This loan service is applicable to components or Engine Controls and Accessories with a current supplier spare parts catalog list price value lower than [value] [currency].}

{In such a case, five [days] Days shall be added to the TAT for the relevant Engine. This slave item shall be removed from the Engine before the Engine shipment.}

{For such loan service, Customer will be charged an amount of [amount] [currency] per missing item and per test cell run. CFM may, at CFM’s sole discretion, provide such loan service to items with higher value, which will be charged at [percent] percent of the current item supplier spare parts price catalog.}

